@findex agent-protect-buffer
@findex agent-kill-session-buffer
The function @code{agent-register-backend} registers an AI tool by constructing an @code{agent-backend} struct from keyword arguments. Backend modules call it at load time. Keywords are validated against the struct's slot names, and the required slots @code{:buffer-p}, @code{:find-all-buffers}, and @code{:start-session} are checked so the shared session layer can rely on a consistent interface.

The full slot set is: identity and presentation (@code{name}, @code{label}, @code{icon}, @code{program}), buffer discovery (@code{buffer-p}, @code{find-all-buffers}, @code{find-buffers-for-dir}), session lifecycle (@code{start-session}, @code{session-identity}, @code{restart-options}), send primitives (@code{send-string}, @code{send-return}, @code{submit}), session state probes (@code{waiting-p}, @code{busy-p}, @code{background-tasks-p}, @code{duration-ms}, @code{display-name-suffix}, @code{notify}), accounts (@code{account-env-var}, @code{accounts}, @code{account-file}, @code{shared-config-items}, @code{canonical-home}, @code{account-init}), skills (@code{run-prompt}, @code{exec-prompt}, @code{skill-roots}, @code{skill-command-prefix}), session history (@code{session-headers}, @code{session-prompt}, @code{resume}, @code{prepare-fork}), integration hooks (@code{sync-theme}), and exit safety (@code{before-exit-ready-to-close-p}, @code{before-kill-check}).

The @code{:start-session} slot starts a new session parameterized by an @code{agent-session} identity struct, optionally with an initial prompt or a resume id. The @code{:session-identity} slot returns a live session buffer's CLI session id, used by @code{agent-restart} to resume in place. @code{agent-start-session} is the core dispatcher that starts a session through its backend's @code{:start-session} function, passing any extra backend-specific options through. The @code{:send-string} slot inserts text into a session's prompt without submitting it, @code{:send-return} submits the pending prompt, and @code{:submit} atomically inserts and submits; the core wrappers @code{agent-send-string}, @code{agent-send-return}, and @code{agent-submit} dispatch through these slots and emit the corresponding session events.

The slots that carry the unified session commands are all optional, and a backend that omits one simply does not support the commands dispatching on it. @code{:resume} resumes a past session, receiving the command's prefix argument, and backs @code{agent-resume}. @code{:session-headers} returns a hash table mapping session id to a plist of @code{:session-id}, @code{:forked-from} and @code{:timestamp}, called with a session buffer and optionally with the one session whose descendants the caller cares about, so a backend that keeps every session in one directory can bound its scan; @code{:session-prompt} enriches one such header with the session's @code{:first-prompt}. Together they back @code{agent-switch-branch} and the branch check before a kill. @code{:prepare-fork} makes a session recorded under one directory visible from another, which is what lets an isolated branch run in a fresh worktree. @code{:exec-prompt} runs a prompt non-interactively and calls back with a plist of @code{:exit-code}, @code{:duration}, @code{:text} and @code{:raw}; @code{agent-batch-todos} runs through it.

@code{agent-display-name} returns a human-readable label for a session buffer. It starts with the project name, adds an instance name when needed to disambiguate duplicates, and lets backends append their own suffixes. The Claude backend uses this to expose branch identity in the modeline and switcher.

@code{agent-parse-skill-frontmatter} reads @samp{SKILL.md} frontmatter shared by Claude and Codex skill runners. It recognizes names, descriptions, argument hints, argument sources, argument choices, defaults, multiplicity, user-invocable flags, and model overrides.

@code{agent-svg-icon} renders SVG strings as inline images, using the current face foreground when the SVG uses @samp{currentColor}. Backends use this for modeline and transient display and can fall back to text abbreviations when SVG rendering is unavailable.

@node Modeline and status helpers
@section Modeline and status helpers

@findex agent-claude-status-model
@findex agent-claude-status-effort
